# emca — the default workspace (docs/emca.md PART SIX). What a namespace
# file will declare once boot is emca's; for now, rc, which is policy exactly
# where policy belongs.
#
# emca starts first, but nothing depends on that: /dev/window/events is a
# QUEUE, so a watcher that arrives late drains the backlog and adopts what it
# finds. And with emca not running at all the windows still open, bare, in
# their types' default panes — emca has no privilege.
emca &
# the home directory, in the left pane — every line a look target
rc /rc/emcaopen directory /usr/kitty >/dev/null
# and three editor windows, which share the main area as TABS: windows of the
# same type, switched. Alternating between two of them is a blink comparator.
rc /rc/emcaopen text /etc/motd >/dev/null
rc /rc/emcaopen text /rc/tour >/dev/null
rc /rc/emcaopen text /usr/kitty/README >/dev/null
